IMPORT prelude

-- Parliamentary Pensions (Abolition) Act 2012 (Singapore) -- who is a Member of Parliament and what is an office (s 2), no pension
-- or gratuity for service on or after 21 May 2011 (s 3), no grant until the person has the minimum service and has ceased to serve
-- (s 4(1), (2)), the stopping, lump-sum catch-up and re-computation of an office-holding Member's pension (s 4(3)), commencement
-- (s 1), and the saving provisions of the Schedule (paras 2-4: assignment and attachment, reduction for corruption, bankruptcy).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PPAA2012.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its Legislative History lists only
-- Act 21 of 2012 itself, with "Commencement: 21 May 2011 (except sections 7 and 8 and the Schedule)", and no later amendment. The
-- Comparative Table says the 2020 Edition's ss 5 and 6 were ss 7 and 8 of Act 21 of 2012; the original ss 5 and 6(1) are
-- "[Omitted as having had effect]".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0260 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short, so it is encoded almost whole. Not encoded: s 4(4) ("subject to sections 13 and 15 of the
-- Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978" -- those sections were not read), the minimum years of reckonable service (they are in ss 3 and 4
-- of the 1978 Act and are taken here as a parameter), s 6 (consequential amendments to three other Acts), Schedule para 5 (pensions
-- charged on the Pension Fund), and how the 1978 Act computes a pension.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers (21 May 2011 is 20110521) so that "on or after" is a comparison of numbers.

§ `Parliamentary Pensions (Abolition) Act 2012 -- pensions`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cut-off date` MEANS 20110521

§§ `1 -- commencement`

-- s 1(1): the Act, "with the exception of sections 5 and 6 and the Schedule, is deemed to have come into operation on 21 May 2011".
-- (2): "Sections 5 and 6 and the Schedule are to come into operation on a date that the Minister appoints by notification in the
-- Gazette." The Act was passed on 10 September 2012 (Legislative History), so ss 2-4 operate retrospectively.
-- The deposit records no such appointed date. s 5 is the repeal of the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978.
DECLARE Provision IS ONE OF
    `section 2 -- interpretation`
    `section 3 -- no pension for service from 21 May 2011`
    `section 4 -- no grant unless service ceases`
    `section 5 -- repeal of the 1978 Act`
    `section 6 -- consequential amendments`
    `the Schedule -- saving provisions`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision, `the Minister has appointed a date by Gazette notification` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date` IS A NUMBER,
      `the appointed date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is in operation on the date` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `section 5 -- repeal of the 1978 Act` THEN `the Minister has appointed a date by Gazette notification` AND `the date` AT LEAST `the appointed date`
    WHEN `section 6 -- consequential amendments` THEN `the Minister has appointed a date by Gazette notification` AND `the date` AT LEAST `the appointed date`
    WHEN `the Schedule -- saving provisions` THEN `the Minister has appointed a date by Gazette notification` AND `the date` AT LEAST `the appointed date`
    OTHERWISE `the date` AT LEAST `the cut-off date`

§§ `2 -- Member of Parliament and office`

-- s 2: "Member of Parliament" means (a) an elected Member (Article 39(1)(a)), (b) a non-constituency Member (Article 39(1)(b)), or
-- (c) a nominated Member (Article 39(1)(c)) of the Constitution.
-- "office" means the office of (a) the Prime Minister; (b) a Deputy Prime Minister; (c) the Speaker; (d) a Senior Minister or a
-- Minister; (e) a Senior Minister of State or a Minister of State; (f) a Mayor; (g) a Senior Parliamentary Secretary or a
-- Parliamentary Secretary; or (h) a Political Secretary.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an elected Member`
    `a non-constituency Member`
    `a nominated Member`
    `a candidate who lost the election`
    `the President`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Member of Parliament` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `an elected Member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a non-constituency Member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nominated Member` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Post IS ONE OF
    `Prime Minister`
    `Deputy Prime Minister`
    `Speaker`
    `Senior Minister`
    `Minister`
    `Senior Minister of State`
    `Minister of State`
    `Mayor`
    `Senior Parliamentary Secretary`
    `Parliamentary Secretary`
    `Political Secretary`
    `Permanent Secretary`
    `Deputy Speaker`

-- A Permanent Secretary and a Deputy Speaker are not in the s 2 list, so neither is an "office" for this Act.
GIVEN `the post` IS A Post
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the post is an office` IF
    CONSIDER `the post`
    WHEN `Permanent Secretary` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Deputy Speaker` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- no pension for service on or after 21 May 2011`

-- s 3: "A pension or gratuity must not be granted under the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978 to any person in respect of -- (a) any
-- service on or after 21 May 2011 in Parliament as a Member of Parliament; or (b) any service on or after 21 May 2011 in any office."
GIVEN `service began on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service can count towards a parliamentary pension` IF
    `service began on` LESS THAN `the cut-off date`

-- The consequence for a person whose service straddles the date: only the part before 21 May 2011 counts.
GIVEN `years served before 21 May 2011` IS A NUMBER, `years served from 21 May 2011` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years that can count towards a parliamentary pension` MEANS
    `years served before 21 May 2011`

§§ `4(1) and (2) -- no grant unless the minimum is reached and the person has ceased to serve`

-- s 4(1): a pension or gratuity "must not be granted on or after 21 May 2011" for service as a Member of Parliament "unless the person
-- -- (a) has not less than the minimum number of years of reckonable service specified in section 3 of that Act to be eligible for a
-- pension under that section; and (b) has ceased at any time thereafter to be a Member of Parliament."
-- (2): the same for service in any office, with the minimum in section 4 of that Act, and "has ceased at any time thereafter to be
-- the holder of any office". The minimum is a PARAMETER here; the 1978 Act was not read for this row.
-- A grant made before 21 May 2011 is outside s 4(1) and (2).
GIVEN `granted on` IS A NUMBER, `years of reckonable service` IS A NUMBER, `minimum years` IS A NUMBER, `has ceased to serve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 allows the grant` IF
        `granted on` LESS THAN `the cut-off date`
    OR  (`years of reckonable service` AT LEAST `minimum years` AND `has ceased to serve`)

§§ `4(3) -- an office-holding Member's pension already granted`

-- s 4(3): where a pension was granted BEFORE 21 May 2011 to an office-holding Member under s 4 of the 1978 Act by virtue of s 5 of
-- that Act, "payment of that pension as a full or reduced pension stops on or after 21 May 2011 and ceases to be payable to that
-- office-holding Member for the period that he or she remains an office-holding Member and any such pension paid in contravention
-- of this subsection must be immediately refunded to the Pension Fund".
GIVEN `granted before 21 May 2011 under section 4 by virtue of section 5 of the 1978 Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date` IS A NUMBER,
      `still an office-holding Member on that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension is stopped on the date` IF
        `granted before 21 May 2011 under section 4 by virtue of section 5 of the 1978 Act`
    AND `the date` AT LEAST `the cut-off date`
    AND `still an office-holding Member on that date`

GIVEN `granted before 21 May 2011 under section 4 by virtue of section 5 of the 1978 Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date` IS A NUMBER,
      `still an office-holding Member on that date` IS A BOOLEAN, `pension was paid for that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment must be refunded to the Pension Fund` IF
        `the pension is stopped on the date` `granted before 21 May 2011 under section 4 by virtue of section 5 of the 1978 Act` `the date` `still an office-holding Member on that date`
    AND `pension was paid for that date`

-- (a): on ceasing to hold office, all the pension that would have been payable between 21 May 2011 and the date of ceasing "(both
-- dates inclusive) is then payable in a lump sum (without interest)".
GIVEN `pension withheld from 21 May 2011 to the date of ceasing` IS A NUMBER, `interest that sum would have earned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lump sum on ceasing to hold office` MEANS
    `pension withheld from 21 May 2011 to the date of ceasing`

-- (b): the pension "is re-computed by adding the period of reckonable service between the date the pension was granted and 20 May
-- 2011 (both dates inclusive) to the period of his or her former reckonable service which had been used in computing his or her
-- pension". Service from 21 May 2011 is not added (s 3).
GIVEN `former reckonable service` IS A NUMBER, `service from the grant to 20 May 2011` IS A NUMBER, `service from 21 May 2011` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the service used in the re-computation` MEANS
    `former reckonable service` PLUS `service from the grant to 20 May 2011`

§§ `Schedule para 2 -- assignment and attachment`

-- Schedule para 2: a pension or gratuity granted under the repealed Act "is not assignable or transferable, except for the purpose
-- of satisfying -- (a) a debt due to the Government; or (b) an order of any court for the payment of periodical sums of money towards
-- the maintenance of the spouse or former spouse or minor child, whether legitimate or not", "and is not liable to be attached,
-- sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim whatever except a debt due to the Government".
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a court maintenance order for a spouse`
    `a court maintenance order for a former spouse`
    `a court maintenance order for a minor child`
    `a bank loan`
    `a judgment debt owed to a private creditor`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension may be assigned to satisfy the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court maintenance order for a spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court maintenance order for a former spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court maintenance order for a minor child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension may be attached for the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Schedule para 3 -- reduction or withholding for corruption`

-- Schedule para 3(1): "The President may reduce or altogether withhold any pension" granted under the repealed Act where the person
-- "has been convicted by any court of an offence (even if only a fine and no term of imprisonment has been imposed) -- (a) under the
-- Prevention of Corruption Act 1960; or (b) involving corruption under any other written law". (2): the President "is to, before
-- exercising any power ... consider the record of the proceedings of the court".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an offence under the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960`
    `an offence involving corruption under another written law`
    `an offence not involving corruption`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `convicted` IS A BOOLEAN, `only a fine was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the President has considered the court record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may reduce or withhold the pension` IF
        `convicted`
    AND `the President has considered the court record`
    AND CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `an offence not involving corruption` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (3): the President may direct all or part of the pension "be applied for the benefit of the person's wife and any child or
-- children, and after the expiry of any term of imprisonment served by the person, also for the person's benefit".
-- INFERENCE: where no imprisonment was imposed there is no term to wait for, so the person may benefit at once.
GIVEN `sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the term has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may apply the pension for the person's own benefit` IF
    (NOT `sentenced to imprisonment`) OR `the term has expired`

§§ `Schedule para 4 -- bankruptcy`

-- Schedule para 4(1): if the pensioner "is adjudged a bankrupt or is declared insolvent by judgment of any court of competent
-- jurisdiction in Singapore or elsewhere, then the pension forthwith ceases". (4): on "a full and proper discharge" the pension "shall
-- be restored to him or her with effect from the date of the discharge".
GIVEN `adjudged bankrupt or declared insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained a full and proper discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension is in payment` IF
    (NOT `adjudged bankrupt or declared insolvent`) OR `obtained a full and proper discharge`

-- (2): while the pension has ceased, the President may direct the moneys to "the person himself and his wife, child or children, or
-- other dependants"; (3): "Moneys applied for the discharge of the debts of the person ... must ... be regarded as applied for the
-- person's benefit."
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `maintenance of the person`
    `maintenance of the wife`
    `maintenance of a child`
    `maintenance of another dependant`
    `paying the person's debts`
    `a gift to a friend who is not a dependant`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may direct the ceased pension to the use` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `a gift to a friend who is not a dependant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
